❯ [38;2;255;255;255mYou are the Autopilot DevOps engineer for this play, preparing repositories for development. Read [38;2;177;185;249mplays/011-show-overlapping-lines/plan.md [38;2;255;255;255m— it states which of the attached      [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mrepositories are part of this play; only touch those.                                                                                                                             [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mEach play is developed on its own branch, [38;2;177;185;249m011-show-overlapping-lines[38;2;255;255;255m, in an isolated git worktree per repository, so several plays can be in progress at once without             [39m  [38;2;255;255;255minterfering. The specs repository ([38;2;177;185;249mmetro[38;2;255;255;255m) is already on that branch — you are working inside its worktree right now, which is why this play's folder is here. Your job is to do   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mthe same for each TARGET CODE repository, under the directory [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011[38;2;255;255;255m.                                                   [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mFor each target repository (its main clone is one of the attached directories — call its path <clone> and its folder name <name>):                                                [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m1. Run [38;2;177;185;249mgit -C <clone> fetch [38;2;255;255;255mso the clone is current.                                                                                                                              [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m2. Create the play worktree at exactly [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011/<name>[38;2;255;255;255m:                                                                   [39m     [38;2;177;185;249mgit -C <clone> worktree add "C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011/<name>" -b 011-show-overlapping-lines                                            [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mHandle these cases without asking me:                                                                                                                                             [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m- If a worktree already exists at [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011/<name>[38;2;255;255;255m, this is a resumed iteration of the same play — leave it as-is and      [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mcontinue; do not recreate it.                                                                                                                                                     [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m- If the branch [38;2;177;185;249m011-show-overlapping-lines [38;2;255;255;255malready exists but has no worktree, add the worktree from that existing branch instead (omit [38;2;177;185;249m-b[38;2;255;255;255m): [38;2;177;185;249mgit -C <clone> worktree add          [39m  [38;2;177;185;249m"C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011/<name>" 011-show-overlapping-lines[38;2;255;255;255m.                                                                             [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m- If a target repository IS the specs repository you are already in, it already has its worktree — skip it.                                                                       [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mOnly stop and ask me how to proceed if something genuinely conflicts — the worktree path is occupied by an unrelated directory, or the repository is in a broken state — do not   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mguess and do not act destructively. Wait for my answer.                                                                                                                           [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mOnce every target repository has its [38;2;177;185;249m011-show-overlapping-lines [38;2;255;255;255mworktree under [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\011[38;2;255;255;255m, end your turn with a short       [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mfactual summary of what you did. That summary must NOT end with a question — only end with a question mark when you are genuinely asking me how to proceed with a real conflict   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mper the rule above.                                                                                                                                                               [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/[38;2;255;255;255m; the documents in [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/ [38;2;255;255;255mare shared by every play and apply to all work. Read    [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: [38;2;177;18